      "writtenOn": "2026-09-21T13:48:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This limit is per HTTP/2 stream, and newHttp2FrameCodec builds on Http2Settings.defaultSettings(), which advertises SETTINGS_MAX_CONCURRENT_STREAMS\u003d100, so the new 10 MiB default allows roughly 1 GiB of buffering per connection against the previous 1.6 MiB - and the aggregator fills before EndpointRoot\u0027s acquirePrincipal runs, so it is reachable unauthenticated. Could we either lower the advertised stream count or document the multiplication on the http-max-request-body-size attribute?",
      "revId": "e420a9b6dec549cf39a0b27a91d44e0a7fd631f9",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
